-- #1114: the "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves" fixture (AGENTS.md's required shape
-- for any new program-global table), NOT another "the fix works" fixture. Six reject_845_*
-- and two reject_792_* fixtures cover the firing case; this one asserts that bindings which
-- must be UNAFFECTED still behave while the new machinery is live all around them.
--
-- ⚠️ EXTENDED after adversarial review, which was right that the first version did not
-- establish its own stated property: it used distinct names and no private bindings, so
-- "if either arm over-copied, this valid program would reject" was a claim the fixture
-- could not have detected. Three assertions now, one per way the wildcard arm could
-- over-copy:
--
--   1. MODULE-MATE — `rid` (no context) shares a module with `qnum` (inferred `Num a =>`).
--      Applied to `NoNum`, which has no `Num` impl. A per-MODULE rather than per-BINDING
--      copy rejects here.
--   2. PRIVATE — `lib/obl1114_q.mdk`'s `hidden` also carries an inferred `Num a =>` and is
--      NOT exported. Resolve already keeps the NAME out of scope, so the local `hidden`
--      below is unambiguously this file's; the risk is the store, which is keyed by name
--      and read cross-module. If a private binding's context enters it, the local
--      `hidden`'s call — at `NoNum`, again with no `Num` — picks up a phantom obligation.
--   3. SHADOWED — the local `hidden` deliberately reuses the private binding's name, which
--      is the only spelling under which a leaked private entry could be reached at all.
--
-- ⚠️ Honest scope note: assertions 2 and 3 are pinned as REGRESSION guards, not as a
-- reproduction. With the store built from `declTopFnNames` (private names included), this
-- exact program still checked clean — the private entry is reached but its stored ids come
-- from the DEFINING module and are absent from the local binding's instantiation subst, so
-- `recordSchemeCallObligations`' #607 all-or-nothing guard skips the predicate whole. That
-- is protection by id mismatch, not by design, and #739 records the same id space COLLIDING
-- across modules — so the store is now filtered to exported names and this fixture pins the
-- filter rather than a defect anyone has reproduced.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUES DERIVED BY HAND, not captured: `rid x = x` is the identity so `rid NoNum`
-- is `NoNum` and `tag` maps it to its pinned string; the local `hidden` is a constant
-- function; `pdisp x = "\{x}"` renders `Int` 5 as `"5"`; `qnum x = x + 1` at `Num Int`
-- gives 6 + 1 = 7. Interpolating a String inserts it verbatim.
import lib.obl1114_p.{pdisp}
import lib.obl1114_q.*

data NoNum = NoNum

tag : NoNum -> String
tag _ = "unrelated"

hidden : NoNum -> String
hidden _ = "shadowed-local"

main = println "\{tag (rid NoNum)} / \{hidden NoNum} / \{pdisp 5} / \{qnum 6}"
